 Most warlocks in Classic WoW are seen with voidwalkers due to their tanking abilities, such as Taunt and AoE taunt (Torment and Suffering), and their Sacrifice shield, which provide survivability for the warlock during solo leveling and questing. While succubi have their uses with damage and crowd control, they lack the defensive capabilities of voidwalkers, making them generally less suitable for leveling. [end of text]


